      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-12-31_WidnesExaminer_art0025" n="art0025">
        <head>BRONCHITIS AD ASTHMA,</head>
        <p>BRONCHITIS AD ASTHMA,</p>
        <p>SUFFLRED MANY YLARS. CURED BY VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE.</p>
        <p>Mr. CLARK., 53, Nerson Street, Aberdeen writes : "I have been suffering many years with chronic bronchitis and asthma. In July last rcommenced taking VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE, I had then been off work six montns. The first dose gave me relief and I rapidly improved. It has indeed made a remarkable change; in fact, I am now cured, anjoying good health, quite a new man; everybody is surprised. For a long time I was in a low state having been weakened by continual vomiting of blood. Your Cougli Care gradually stopped the vomiting. I cannot realise, after so much doctoring and suffering how you Cough Cure has cured me so quickly." V.D;O'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE is the most efficient remedy procurable for c oughs, colds, bronchitis, asthma, catarrh, weak lungs ond children's coughs. 91d., is. lid. and 2s. 9d. at Chemists everywhere.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-12-31_WidnesExaminer_art0026" n="art0026">
        <head>HOCKEY.</head>
        <p>HOCKEY.</p>
        <p>CHESTER v. STOCKTON HEATH.</p>
        <p>Played at Chester. From the bully-off even play resulted, each side attacking in turn. At last, after a. grand run by Baxter, W. Richardson, opened the scor- ing for Stockton Heath. Chester attacked strongly, but sound play by the Stockton backs, L. Fairclough and E. Pierpoint, kept them at bay. From a bully on the Stockton goal line W. Richardson got the ball and ran between the Chester backs and safely placed the ball in the net. Half-time score—Stockton, 2; Chester, nil. After changing ends, Chester took up the attack and a misunderstanding between the Stockton backs and goal- keeper, allowed the home team scored. Final: Stockton Heath, 2; Chester, 1.</p>
      </div>
