        <p>Warrington Poachers at Runcorn. At Runcorn Petty Sessions on Tuesday, James Holden Sand John Lee, labourers, of Plumpton-street Warrington, and Henry Johnson, of Shepherd-street Warrington, were summoned for poaching on the estate of Sir Richard Brooke, at Norton, on December 17. The defendants pleaded guilty. Evidence was given that Detective Motherhead and Police-constables Bailey and Cameron met the defendant in Warrington road at 4 a.m. Each w provided with a complete 'poacher's outfit, but they had only one rabbit, which was in Holden's bag. The defendants pleaded that they had been out of work for many weeks, and borrowed the nets in order to make a shilling or two for their starving wives and children. They were novices at the game, and only caught one rabbit. Superintendent Ennion said both Holden and Johnson had previously been convicted of trespassing in pursuit of game. These mcLn were each fined 10s. and costs Os. 6d., and Lee was fined ss. tnd costs 9s. 6d.</p>
      </div>
