      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-12-31_WidnesExaminer_art0068" n="art0068">
        <head>DR. HonToN'i PRESIDENTIAL PROGRAMME.</head>
        <p>DR. HonToN'i PRESIDENTIAL PROGRAMME.</p>
        <p>Rev: fir. R. F. Horton becomes the President of the National Council of the Evangelical Free Churches in March of next year in succession to Rev. F. B. I.lreyer, B.A. Dr. 'Horton has decided to get into touch with the whole of Nonconformity throughout the country by means of special Conventions at various centres. These centres will be eight in number and include Plymouth, Llandrindod Wells, , Hexham, L owestoft, Oxford, Harrogate, London, and Nottingham. The Conventions will extend over three days—Tuesday, Wednesday. and Thursday. Dr. Horton will preach on the preceding Sunday in the pulpits of two different denominations. Representatives from all the Councils in the different areas will attend. _ . .</p>
        <p>The programme includes a Sunrise prayer meeting at 'T.3O each morning, Conferences each morning at 11, "Confession of sin," "Consecration," and "The Work of the Holy Spirit," and in the afternoons on " Aggressive Christian work." "Work for young men and young women," "Free Churchrouncil Work." On Tuesday evening a special sermon will be preached. Wednesday will be devoted to a great united meeting for young people and on Thursday evening there will be a public meeting on "The Awakening of the Free Churches." In addition to Dr. Horton Rev. F. B. Meyer, 8.A., Rev. Th•nnas Law, Rev. R. J. Campbell, M.A., Rev. Dr. Campbell Morgan, M.A., will take part in these Conven- tions and it is expected that Rev. J. H. Jowett, M.A. , will also attend:</p>
      </div>
