      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-12-31_WidnesExaminer_art0169" n="art0169">
        <head>Hockey. [By R.G.P.]</head>
        <p>Hockey. [By R.G.P.]</p>
        <p>Stockton Heath first eleven journeyed to Chester last week and defeated the Chester team by 2-1. The score. about represents the play, although the Chester goal should certainly have been saved. The first goal was obtained by W. Richatdson, after S. Baxter had run half the length of the field, while just before half-time W. Richardson scored again, after running more than three-quarters of the length of the field.</p>
        <p>E. Pierpoint at back played a fine game, and was about the best man on the field, his hitting being clean and powerful while his tackling left nothing to be wished for.</p>
        <p>The second team match was cancelled, as were most of the important matches. On Boxing Day morning the second eleven played the Royal Club," and were defeated by 3-1. The Royal played a good combined bustling game, and on the days play were quite two goals better than the home side.</p>
        <p>The result came as a surprises as after Latchford H. had beaten the visitors the previous week by no less than 4-1, the home side (on paper) seemed to have an easy thing on.</p>
        <p>Below I give the record of the club up-to-date. Goals P. W. L. D. F 3r. Agst. Stockton Heath I Stockton Heath II l2 ... 5 ... ... 1 ... 37 ... 2a</p>
        <p>corers : . , Ist Team. Matches. Goals. R. Pierpoint W. Richardson H. Kirkconnell C. H. Bond S. Baxter w. Longdin 2 Eric Fairclough 7</p>
        <p>44 2nd Team. Matches. Goals: W. Longdin ll D. Skelton W. Richardson W. Howard R. Fairclough 1 A. Jones R. Monks 2 R. Pierpoint 2</p>
        <p>To-day Stockton Heath play Sale I. and IL, when the following teams will represent Stockton Heath : First team (at Sale), R. G. Pierpoint, goal);( L. Fair- dough and E. Pierpoint, hacks; J. Richardson, IL liirkconnel and G. Hatton, halves; C. H. Bond, R. Monks, W. Longdin, W. Richardson and R. Fairclough, forwards. Train leaves Arpley at 1-13. Referee, Mr. R. M. Roberts.</p>
        <p>Second team (at home), F. G. Kirtland, goal ‘. P. B. Hasvtin (capt.). and J. Cliff e. backs: E. Fairclough. H. Smith and L. Robertson. halves; C. R. Hartley, W. Howard, H.Dolan,T.Crompton and D.Skelton, forwards. Bully off 2.30. Referee Mr. N. W. Bellamy.</p>
        <p>The following are the results of some of the local matches, the home club being first : Chester 1, Stockton Heath 2. 3Lancashire 2. Cheshire 0. Latchford "New members" 6, Latchford "Old Bo ys" 4. Stocktov Heath 2nd 1, The Royal 3.</p>
